{"kind":"driver:amendment","task":"1","amends":"clause","what":"The Context sentence \"`examLandings` (line 3340, `proofTests.map(landingOf)`) are in scope\" at the exam-run site: the landings are recomputed inside `runExam` as `proofTests.map(landingOf)` rather than read from the `examLandings` const.","why":"`examLandings` is declared with `const` at BASE line 3340, but `runExam` is CALLED at lines 3161 and 3212 — the pre-review pass and its one re-run — which is before that declaration is evaluated. Reading the binding there is a temporal-dead-zone throw on every task with a runnable exam. `landingOf` is an outer-scope const from line 2468 and `proofTests` is in scope, so the recomputation is the same value the clause names.","id":"01M2MK5YBF0000PXB4HK8T1QM9","ts":1789545085295}
