{"kind":"driver:amendment","task":"3","amends":"clause","what":"M2's `detail` is spelled `hollow: <stem> left its mutant <path> alive — the exam did not catch the wrong state`, and a row whose `mutant_killed` is `null` (a `mutant.json` that was missing or unparsable) appends nothing. The line is also de-duplicated per exam stem, so a second review round that re-reads the same record does not post it twice.","why":"The clause fixes only that the detail begins `hollow:` and names the stem and the mutant path; it says `mutant_killed` `false` and `true` and is silent on `null`, which `stateExamRowsOf` writes for an absent file — an absence is not a survivor, so it says nothing. The per-stem dedup keeps leg (d)'s \"one `driver:finding`\" true on a task that also takes an exam-rejected round.","id":"01M2MK848700004JCS1QHF1P7D","ts":1789545156871}
{"kind":"driver:amendment","task":"3","amends":"clause","what":"M1's `actor` falls back to `implementer` when the round's blocking issue carries none — which is every issue the driver itself minted (a red `Run:`, a red exam, a red `Check:`).","why":"`REVIEWER_SCHEMA` does not require `actor`, and the driver-minted blocking issues appended before plan routing carry no actor at all, so the event would otherwise have an undefined field. `implementer` is the actor those reds are routed to everywhere else in the round.","id":"01M2MK84870001G43MSCN3SBT0","ts":1789545156871}
{"kind":"driver:amendment","task":"3","amends":"files","what":"`fleet/run-engine.mjs`: `examLandings` was moved from the review round (its old site at the `examPathIn` comment) up beside `examRunnable`, and a new `examLandingPaths()` sits with it; `examPathIn` is re-expressed over the new module-level `pathTokensIn` while keeping its first-match-in-token-order answer.","why":"M3 case (i) fires at the pre-review pass, long before the review round — reading `examLandings` there while it was still declared at the round would be a temporal-dead-zone error. The move is within the file the task already owns; it is noted because it relocates a declaration the Context named by line.","id":"01M2MK84870002YDM413SJTZ9G","ts":1789545156871}
