{"kind":"driver:amendment","task":"7","amends":"clause","what":"fleet/publish-fold.mjs — the `tip unmoved` short circuit now reads `if (prior && prior.disposition !== 'conflict parked' && prior.tip && prior.tip === tip)`, so a prior attempt that PARKED no longer short-circuits a later attempt on the same tip.","why":"M3's leg (c) drives attempt 2 on an unmoved tip after a parked attempt 1, and the Context states it 'folds afresh ... onto the same tip, meets the same conflict, and dispatches resolve:publish-fold:2:1:1'. At BASE the guard fired first and returned 'tip unmoved' with no resolver dispatched and no attempt-2 brief at all, so no wiring of mine could have produced the brief leg (c) reads. The guard's own comment already says 'the attempt that already folded', and a parked attempt reached no candidate. Inert in production: sandbox-boot.sh only dispatches attempt 2 after a push 405, which only follows a folded attempt 1.","id":"01M2MM106G0000P7Q9BS7PR40W","ts":1789545971920}
